      "title": "dfilter: Allow character constants in arithmetic",
      "message": "dfilter: Allow character constants in arithmetic\n\nwireshark-filter says that character constants can be used as\nintegers. Allow them in arithmetic, instead of aborting:\n\n$ ./run/dftest -s \"udp.dstport == 66+'\\x01' \"\nFilter:\n udp.dstport == 66+'\\x01'\n\nSyntax tree:\n 0 TEST_ANY_EQ:\n   1 FIELD(udp.dstport <FT_UINT16>)\n   1 FVALUE(67 <FT_UINT16>)\n\nInstructions:\n 0000 READ_TREE        udp.dstport      -> R0\n 0001 IF_FALSE_GOTO    3\n 0002 ANY_EQ           R0 == 67\n 0003 RETURN\n\nInstead of:\n\n$ ./run/dftest -s \"udp.dstport == 66+'\\x01'\"\nFilter:\n udp.dstport == 66+'\\x01'\n\n ** (dftest:351008) 09:32:22.558983 [DFilter ERROR] epan/dfilter/semcheck.c:2068 -- check_arithmetic(): Invalid syntax node type 'CHARCONST'.\n ** (dftest:351008) Aborting on fatal log level exception\nAborted (core dumped)\n",
